---
alwaysApply: false
description : How to handle deletion (soft-delete) and archived item
---

Each table should include a deleted_dt column (timestamptz) in Supabase. When an item is deleted, set this value to now(). You can use the helper function handleSoftDeleteItem from utils/SupabaseUtils.tsx for this purpose.

Functions such as fetchDocs (in utils/SupabaseUtils.tsx) and updateOrInsertInListWithId (in utils/Utils.tsx) automatically exclude items where deleted_dt is not null, ensuring deleted items are not fetched or updated.

No RLS rules should apply during deletion — for security and backup reasons, we only use soft deletion. Note that users should not be able to restore deleted items.

If you need to allow archiving (so items can later be unarchived), add another column archived_dt (timestamptz) to the table. You can use the helper functions handleArchivedItem and handleUnArchivedItem from utils/SupabaseUtils.tsx to manage this behavior.